  "docTitle": "Monotonic deque - SDE Prep Dojo",
  "description": "Monotonic deque deep dive: sliding window maximum, two deques for longest subarray with max - min <= limit, a deque over prefix sums for the shortest subarray with sum at least K, and deque-optimised DP (Jump Game VI), with steppers and Go, C++, Java and Python templates.",
  "hero": {
    "tag": "header",
    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\r\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\"><span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"4\">Level 4 - Advanced</span><span class=\"time\">45 min</span><span class=\"chip\">Deep dive</span><span class=\"chip\">O(n) amortised</span><span class=\"chip\">Sliding window + prefix sums</span></div>\r\n  <h1>Monotonic deque</h1>\r\n  <p class=\"lead\">Get the maximum (or minimum) of a moving window in O(1) per step by keeping only the values that can still win. Sliding window maximum, two deques for \"max - min &lt;= limit\", a deque over prefix sums for the shortest subarray with sum at least K (negatives allowed), and the same trick speeding up a DP. Templates in Go, C++, Java and Python.</p>\r\n"
  },
